<Layout
	title="About Jitendra Verma"
	description="Jitendra Verma — a Computer Science engineer and developer building mobile and web apps, writing technical guides, and contributing to open source."
	pubDate={new Date('January 1 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		Hi, I'm <strong>Jitendra Verma</strong> — a Computer Science and Engineering student at Uka Tarsadia University, Surat, and a developer who likes turning ideas into shipped apps. I work across mobile and web: Flutter and Dart for cross-platform apps, Swift and SwiftUI on iOS, and React, Next.js, and ASP.NET Core on the web.
	</p>

	<p>
		Most of my time goes into building products end to end. I built <strong>SecureVault</strong>, a privacy vault disguised as everyday utility apps with AES-256 encryption and native platform-channel tricks like dynamic app-icon switching; <strong>Chain Reaction MAX</strong>, a multiplayer strategy game with real-time state on Riverpod; and <strong>2ndThought</strong>, a cognitive app-blocker grounded in System 1 vs System 2 psychology. On the web, I've shipped an e-commerce site and a TMDB-powered iOS app for discovering movies and shows.
	</p>

	<p>
		I also enjoy writing and giving back. As a <strong>Technical Content Writer at GeeksforGeeks</strong>, I wrote installation and how-to guides focused on macOS and developer tooling — many of those articles live on GeeksforGeeks, and you'll find them linked from my <a href="/blog">blog</a>. In open source, I've contributed adaptive loss functions to <strong>SciML / NeuralPDE.jl</strong> and a theme system with dark mode to <strong>TuringLang</strong>'s documentation sites.
	</p>

	<p>
		Outside of code, I'm into design and creative tools — Figma, Canva, Lightroom, and DaVinci Resolve. In 2024, my team was a finalist at the <strong>Smart India Hackathon</strong>.
	</p>

	<p>
		Want to build something or just say hi? Reach me at
		<a href="mailto:jitendravjh@gmail.com">jitendravjh@gmail.com</a>, or find me on
		<a href="https://github.com/jitendravjh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a> and
		<a href="https://linkedin.com/in/jitendravjh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
